    The word search form (FIND-10).

    A plain GET form with no JavaScript at all: submitting it navigates, which
    is why search works with scripting disabled and why the result is a real,
    linkable URL. `role="search"` gives assistive technology the landmark, and
    the label is a real <label> rather than a placeholder, which disappears the
    moment someone starts typing.

    Locals: variantCode, and optionally value. %>
<form class="search" action="/search" method="get" role="search">
  <input type="hidden" name="variant" value="<%= variantCode %>">
  <label class="search__label" for="search-q">Look up a word</label>
  <div class="search__row">
    <input
      class="search__input"
      id="search-q"
      type="search"
      name="q"
      value="<%= typeof value === 'undefined' ? '' : value %>"
      placeholder="cupcake"
      autocomplete="off"
      autocapitalize="none"
      spellcheck="false"
      enterkeyhint="search"
    >
    <button class="search__submit" type="submit">Search</button>
  </div>
</form>
